  "verbalization": "Tiapride is shown to have a target relationship with CCRF-HSB-2 through two distinct pathways. In one pathway, Tiapride targets Inosine-5'-monophosphate dehydrogenase 2, which in turn is targeted by a complex compound with a specific chemical structure, and this complex ultimately targets CCRF-HSB-2. In the second pathway, Tiapride directly targets Valacyclovir hydrolase, which is also targeted by a complex compound, and this complex again targets CCRF-HSB-2. Both pathways suggest that Tiapride exerts its effects through interactions with compounds that are involved in the metabolism or signaling of CCRF-HSB-2. The evidence supports a mechanism where Tiapride influences CCRF-HSB-2 through the modulation of these target enzymes, potentially by inhibiting their activity or altering their interaction with the cell. The integration of these pathways highlights the role of these enzymes in the biological process that connects Tiapride to CCRF-HSB-2.",
